{"id":"a0c1fcc0-c579-4a4d-9a6e-5c858f3f0049","object":"chat.completion","created":1785009744,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if 'threshold' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Payload must contain 'threshold' and 'calls'\\\")\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"'calls' must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        # Validate each call has required fields\\n        required_call_fields = ['call_id', 'loss_without_call', 'loss_with_call', 'prediction_tokens', 'parseable']\\n        if not all(field in call for field in required_call_fields):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call missing one of {required_call_fields}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n\\n        if tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive, got {tokens}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'accepted': accepted,\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\\n        })\\n\\n    return {\\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that implements the task described. The task is \"api_call_loss_filter\". Based on the description and the fixtures, the case has:\n- threshold: number\n- calls: list of objects each with call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable (boolean)\n\nFor each call:\n- gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n- normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (since \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" So divide by prediction_tokens)\n- Then the call is accepted if parseable is true AND normalized_gain >= threshold (inclusive threshold, so >=)\n- Also \"stronger_counterfactual\" is not explicitly defined; it may just be using the comparison (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) as the gain. The description says \"weighted losses, the stronger counterfactual\" but we only have loss_without and loss_with. So just compute difference.\n- \"normalized_weights\" might refer to dividing by prediction_tokens.\n\nThen output:\n- accepted_call_ids: list of call_id strings in the order they appear in the original calls list (stable order)\n- diagnostics: list of objects with accepted (boolean), call_id (string), normalized_gain (number) for each call in the same order.\n\nThe normalized_gain should be rounded? The requirement: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" Not specified rounding precision. In the fixture examples, we see loss values with many decimals. The output schema says normalized_gain type is number. We can round to say 6 decimal places? But not specified. The instruction: \"Return only JSON-serializable values\" and \"rounded per-call diagnostics.\" We can simply compute the float; JSON will serialize it. But perhaps we need to round to some precision? Since it's a number, it's fine. But to be safe, we can round to, say, 8 decimal places or just leave as float. The input values have 8 decimals typically. I'll compute as float and not round explicitly, because JSON serialization preserves floating point representation. However, to avoid floating point artifacts, rounding to a reasonable number of decimals might be expected. The examples don't show expected output. I'll assume we compute normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens and keep as float. The diagnostics should be in same order as input calls.\n\nThe function must not mutate case. Use standard library only.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case) that receives the payload (with 'threshold' and 'calls'). Validate that required fields exist. If not, raise ValueError. For each call, compute. Then build result.\n\nEdge cases: prediction_tokens could be zero? In the fixture they are all positive >=2. But to be safe, if prediction_tokens <=0, normalized_gain undefined; but task says \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" So prediction_tokens should be >=1. If not, maybe raise ValueError? We'll assume input is valid.\n\nAlso the \"parseable\" field is boolean.\n\nReturn JSON object with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nNow, produce final answer as a JSON object with single key \"implementation\" containing Python source code as a string (escaped). Ensure the code is properly indented.\n\nI'll write the code with clear steps. Use float division.\n\nMake sure to handle missing fields: raise ValueError.\n\nI'll also include a docstring.\n\nNow, produce output."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2171,"completion_tokens":1140,"total_tokens":3311,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":731},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":123},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}